==Quick Walkthrough==
#Ask the [[Blades:Shulkunaak|dragon]] about the Sorcerer-King.

==Detailed Walkthrough==
This quest is started after The Haunted Forest:

====Saashi====
:''Now that you have recovered the Elder Scroll, it is only a matter of time before the Sorcerer-King comes to take it back.''
::'''It'll take some time before he's ready.'''
:::''We need to move quickly. This town cannot withstand an undead assault.''
:::''Saashi once met someone while traveling... They might know how to use the Elder Scroll against the Sorcerer-King.''<small> (see dialogue box below) </small>
::'''What should we do next?'''
:::''Saashi once met someone while traveling... They might know how to use the Elder Scroll against the Sorcerer-King.'' <small> (see dialogue box below) </small>

All paths lead to
:::''Saashi once met someone while traveling... They might know how to use the Elder Scroll against the Sorcerer-King.''
:::''You might not be too keen on talking to him, though.''
:::'''Why is that?'''
:::''Well... he is a dragon. Shulkunaak. This one recognized his name in those runic inscriptions.''
:::'''You met a dragon?'''
:::''It is a long story. But Saashi promises to tell once this is all over.''
:::''This one believes he can help figure it out. If he does not kill you first, that is.''
::::'''All right, let's go then.'''
:::::''Saashi will start packing.'' <small>(starts quest MQ17)</small>
::::'''I need to think about it.'''
:::::''This one understands, but... it may be our only hope at this point.''

Should you decline and talk to Saashi again, she will insist again to talk to Shulkunaak:
:''Shulkunaak helped bind the Sorcerer-King back when he was first defeated.''
:''This one believes he can help figure it out. If he does not kill you first, that is.''
::'''All right, let's go then.'''
:::''Saashi will start packing.'' <small>(starts quest MQ17)</small>
::'''I need to think about it.'''
:::''This one understands, but... it may be our only hope at this point.''

If you accept, and talk to Saashi again, she will say the following line:
:''Saashi still thinks asking the dragon Shulkunaak is our best plan.''

You are ready to continue the quest. Choose Facing the Dragon from the quest map and enter the dungeon.

===Facing the Dragon===
When you arrive at the cave, you will see Saashi who can be spoken to:

:''The dragon Shulkunaak should be somewhere in this cave complex.''
:''Just please, be respectful when you meet him. This one would be very sad if he ended up eating you.''

If you speak to her again:
:''Are you having second thoughts? We could always go back to town...''


Head onwards through the cave, until eventually you will have to fight two [[Blades:Cave Spider|cave spiders]]. As you enter the large area with two cave bears, head to the right for the '''secret area''', the lever is on the cave wall and looks like a torch. This will open up the secret area behind a rock which contains healing food and a silver chest. 

Once you have finished with the secret area, continue onwards and you will have to kill a giant cave spider and spider. You will reach a large opening with dragon skeletons strewn about, there are another two cave bears in here to deal with, however there is a chance of there being food in the form of mushrooms in this area. Going forwards, you will have to deal with another giant cave spider, before eventually reaching an opening with Shulkunaak. Speak to Shulkunaak. His dialogue tree is complex and revolves around raising or lowering an internal flag called (GenericQuestNPCFlag). Different options are available given more aggressive or more respectful paths:

====Shulkunaak====
:''Who dares disturb my peace? Speak, {{hover|intruder|volaan}}. Your life hangs in the balance.''
::'''I am <Player Name>, and I seek your wisdom.'''
::''You came here alone? That was very brave, or very stupid.''
:::'''I'm not afraid of you.'''
:::''{{hover|bravery|Ahkrin}} - bravery - may impress your peers. All it will earn you here is a quick death.''
:::'''I trust your good judgement with my life.'''
:::''Stupidity it is, then. If it is death you seek, I will give it to you.''
::'''I am <Player Name>, and I don't fear you!'''
::''Do you think it wise to provoke me, here in my own lair?''
:::'''I see no other option for a coward like you.'''
:::''Do not think you can provoke me that easily. But I admire your bravado.''
:::'''I am told dragons appreciate confidence.'''
:::''Your {{hover|bravery|ahkrin}} - bravery - has earned my respect. But that will not save your life.''

Both will lead to:
:''"But first, tell me. Why did you come all the way here to die?"''
:'''The Sorcerer-king Celemaril has returned.'''

You can choose to continue talking to Shulkunaak to gain the information, or begin a fight for it.

